# _redirects  (place at repo ROOT)
# Works on BOTH Netlify and Cloudflare Pages
#
# Netlify:  uses this to 301-redirect all traffic → CF
# Cloudflare Pages: reads _redirects too, but we leave
#           it empty of real rules so CF just serves the site.
#
# HOW THIS WORKS:
#   - Netlify sees this file and redirects visitors to CF.
#   - Cloudflare Pages also reads _redirects but the rule
#     below only fires on the Netlify host, so CF ignores it
#     and serves the site normally.
#
# ⚠️  Replace "mstvnet.pages.dev" with your actual CF domain
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Redirect ALL Netlify traffic to Cloudflare (permanent)
https://apnatv.netlify.app/*   https://crickethd.pages.dev/:splat   301!
http://apnatv.netlify.app/*    https://crickethd.pages.dev/:splat   301!

# SPA fallback for Cloudflare (harmless on Netlify since it 301s first)
/channels_pages/*   /index.html   200
